Limitations
Because particles are simulated on the GPU, they are also stateless. This means that they don't interact with the game world -- once they're generated, their trajectories are fixed. As a result, particles won't be able to interact with ships or projectiles in either direction -- they can't affect the game state and they can't be affected by the game state.

OpenGL 4.3 support, as well as compatibility profile support, is required. Note that the latter is more likely to be an issue on systems that have deprecated OpenGL, such as Macs.

